# cargo's build directory: generated, machine-specific, rewritten every build.
# Tracked once by accident -- 279 files, 35.7 MB (RUSTIUM curse R5).
# The ignore must exist BEFORE the first build; afterwards only
# `git rm -r --cached Gos/target` evicts it (Curse 32, the Sticky Track).
/target

# the verifier's certificate is a RECEIPT, regenerated by:
#   py -3 verify_rustium.py
# Its sha256 must not move between runs (Curse 38). Keep it out of the tree so
# a stale copy can never be mistaken for a fresh one.
rustium_certificate.json

# -- RUN EXPORTS: the HELENA doctrine, applied (Curse 31 / R5) ---------------
# A single EXPORT writes ~23 MB: frame.bits is EIGHT bytes on disk per byte of
# payload, on purpose (1s and 0s cost what they cost). Four clicks made 88 MB.
#
# So: the heavy payload is LOCAL and never enters git; git tracks only the tiny
# MANIFEST mirror, which carries the digests, the caps and the truncation flags
# -- the steps, not the payload. Another mage regenerates by pressing the
# button. "Pay thea Heleni in compute."
/runs/**
!/runs/**/
!/runs/**/MANIFEST.json
!/runs/**/SESSION.json
!/runs/**/SHOTS.log

# Rendered output from `cargo run --example ...` lands in the crate root.
# Ignored as a CLASS, not name by name: enumerating `c60_*.png` already missed
# `dashboard_skeleton.png` within the hour, which is R11's lesson again -- a
# rule that has to be extended per artifact is not a rule.
# Regenerate with:  cargo run --example paint_c60 / paint_dashboard
/*.png
/*.ppm
/*.bits
/*.bin

**/*.rs.bk

# witness build products -- regenerated by witnesses/run_all.ps1
experiments/witnesses/*.exe
